{"qid":"Q186537","names":["Khanate of Kazan"],"title":"Khanate of Kazan","endonym":{"native":"Qazan xanlığı","lang":"tt-latn"},"capsule":"The Khanate of Kazan emerged c. 1438 when Ulugh Muhammad, expelled from the Golden Horde, established an independent Tatar state at the confluence of the Volga and Kazanka rivers on the territory of former Volga Bulgaria. At its greatest extent it dominated the middle Volga, Ural, and western Siberian trade routes, with a population of Tatars, Chuvash, Mari, Udmurt, and Mordvin peoples. After decades of Muscovite pressure and internal dynastic conflict, Ivan IV besieged and stormed Kazan on 2 October 1552, incorporating the khanate into the growing Russian state and ending Tatar political independence in the Volga region.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core territorial extent around the middle Volga is well established from Russian chronicle and diplomatic records; outer tributary zones fluctuated and are less precisely mapped.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Khanate of Kazan","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Khanate-of-Kazan"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Khanate of Kazan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khanate_of_Kazan"},{"label":"Encyclopaedia Iranica: Kazan Khanate","url":"https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/kazan-khanate"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Khanate of Kazan","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Ulugh Muhammad","nativeName":"Олуг Мөхәммәд","roman":"Uluğ Möxämmäd","start":1438,"end":1445,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mahmud (Mahmudek)","nativeName":"Мәхмүд","roman":"Mäxmüd","sta